msgstr "``TypeError``"

#: ../../../builtins-hard.rst:79 ../../../builtins-hard.rst:234
#: ../../../builtins-hard.rst:492
msgid "``1``"
msgstr "``1``"

#: ../../../builtins-hard.rst:84
msgid ""
"``True == 1`` and equal objects must hash equally, so ``hash(True)`` and "
"``hash(1)`` are both ``1``."
msgstr ""
"``True == 1`` y los objetos iguales deben tener el mismo hash, así que "
"``hash(True)`` y ``hash(1)`` valen ambos ``1``."

#: ../../../builtins-hard.rst:101
#, python-brace-format
msgid "``{True: 'a', 1: 'b'}``"
msgstr "``{True: 'a', 1: 'b'}``"

#: ../../../builtins-hard.rst:102
#, python-brace-format
msgid "``{1: 'b'}``"
msgstr "``{1: 'b'}``"

#: ../../../builtins-hard.rst:103
#, python-brace-format
msgid "``{True: 'b'}``"
msgstr "``{True: 'b'}``"

#: ../../../builtins-hard.rst:104
#, python-brace-format
msgid "``{True: 'a'}``"
msgstr "``{True: 'a'}``"

#: ../../../builtins-hard.rst:109
msgid ""
"Because ``True == 1`` and they hash the same, the dict treats them as one "
"key. The *first* key inserted (``True``) is kept, but the later assignment "
"overwrites its value with ``'b'``."
msgstr ""
"Como ``True == 1`` y tienen el mismo hash, el diccionario los trata como una"
" única clave. Se conserva la *primera* clave insertada (``True``), pero la "
"asignación posterior sobrescribe su valor con ``'b'``."

#: ../../../builtins-hard.rst:129 ../../../builtins-hard.rst:156
msgid "``nan``"
msgstr "``nan``"

#: ../../../builtins-hard.rst:130 ../../../builtins-hard.rst:155
#: ../../../builtins-hard.rst:312 ../../../builtins-hard.rst:385
#: ../../../builtins-hard.rst:466
msgid "``ValueError``"
msgstr "``ValueError``"

#: ../../../builtins-hard.rst:135
msgid ""
"IEEE-754 defines NaN as unequal to everything, including itself, so the "
"comparison is ``False``."
msgstr ""
"IEEE-754 define NaN como distinto de todo, incluido de sí mismo, así que la "
"comparación es ``False``."

#: ../../../builtins-hard.rst:161
msgid ""
"Even though ``nan != nan``, membership tests short-circuit on *identity* "
"first (``x is element or x == element``). The list holds the same object, so"
" the identity check succeeds and ``in`` returns ``True``."
msgstr ""
"Aunque ``nan != nan``, las comprobaciones de pertenencia hacen cortocircuito"
" primero por *identidad* (``x is element or x == element``). La lista "
"contiene el mismo objeto, así que la comprobación de identidad tiene éxito e"
" ``in`` devuelve ``True``."

#: ../../../builtins-hard.rst:179
msgid "``-1 -2 -3``"
msgstr "``-1 -2 -3``"

#: ../../../builtins-hard.rst:180
msgid "``0 -1 -2``"
msgstr "``0 -1 -2``"

#: ../../../builtins-hard.rst:181
msgid "``-1 -1 -2``"
msgstr "``-1 -1 -2``"

#: ../../../builtins-hard.rst:182
msgid "``0 -2 -2``"
msgstr "``0 -2 -2``"

#: ../../../builtins-hard.rst:187
msgid ""
"Banker's rounding also works on negatives: ``-0.5`` -> ``0``, ``-1.5`` -> "
"``-2``, ``-2.5`` -> ``-2`` — each snapped to the nearest even integer."
msgstr ""
"El redondeo bancario también funciona con negativos: ``-0.5`` -> ``0``, "
"``-1.5`` -> ``-2``, ``-2.5`` -> ``-2`` — cada uno ajustado al entero par más"
" cercano."

#: ../../../builtins-hard.rst:205
msgid "``2.68``"
msgstr "``2.68``"

#: ../../../builtins-hard.rst:206
msgid "``2.7``"
msgstr "``2.7``"

#: ../../../builtins-hard.rst:207
msgid "``2.67``"
msgstr "``2.67``"

#: ../../../builtins-hard.rst:208
msgid "``2.675``"
msgstr "``2.675``"

#: ../../../builtins-hard.rst:213
msgid ""
"``2.675`` cannot be stored exactly; the nearest ``float`` is slightly "
"*below* ``2.675``, so rounding to two places gives ``2.67`` rather than the "
"\"textbook\" ``2.68``. Banker's rounding is irrelevant here — the stored "
"value simply is not a true half."
msgstr ""
"``2.675`` no se puede almacenar de forma exacta; el ``float`` más cercano "
"queda ligeramente *por debajo* de ``2.675``, así que redondear a dos "
"decimales da ``2.67`` en lugar del ``2.68`` \"de manual\". El redondeo "
"bancario es irrelevante aquí — el valor almacenado sencillamente no es un "
"medio exacto."

#: ../../../builtins-hard.rst:232 ../../../builtins-hard.rst:464
msgid "``-1``"
msgstr "``-1``"

#: ../../../builtins-hard.rst:233
msgid "``-2``"
msgstr "``-2``"

#: ../../../builtins-hard.rst:235 ../../../builtins-hard.rst:387
#: ../../../builtins-hard.rst:463
msgid "``0``"
msgstr "``0``"

#: ../../../builtins-hard.rst:240
msgid ""
"In CPython, ``-1`` is reserved internally to signal an error from "
"``__hash__``, so the hash of the integer ``-1`` is remapped to ``-2``."
msgstr ""
"En CPython, ``-1`` está reservado internamente para señalar un error de "
"``__hash__``, así que el hash del entero ``-1`` se reasigna a ``-2``."

#: ../../../builtins-hard.rst:257
msgid "``[False, 0, True, 1]``"
msgstr "``[False, 0, True, 1]``"

#: ../../../builtins-hard.rst:258
msgid "``[False, 0, 1, True]``"
msgstr "``[False, 0, 1, True]``"

#: ../../../builtins-hard.rst:259
msgid "``[0, False, 1, True]``"
msgstr "``[0, False, 1, True]``"

#: ../../../builtins-hard.rst:260
msgid "``[True, 1, False, 0]``"
msgstr "``[True, 1, False, 0]``"

#: ../../../builtins-hard.rst:265
msgid ""
"Since ``False == 0`` and ``True == 1``, sorting compares equal values and "
"Python's sort is *stable*: it preserves the input order within each equal "
"group. ``False`` precedes ``0`` and ``True`` precedes ``1`` exactly as they "
"appeared."
msgstr ""
"Como ``False == 0`` y ``True == 1``, la ordenación compara valores iguales y"
" la ordenación de Python es *estable*: conserva el orden de entrada dentro "
"de cada grupo de iguales. ``False`` precede a ``0`` y ``True`` precede a "
"``1`` exactamente como aparecían."

#: ../../../builtins-hard.rst:284
#, python-brace-format
msgid "``{1, True, 1.0}``"
msgstr "``{1, True, 1.0}``"

#: ../../../builtins-hard.rst:285
#, python-brace-format
msgid "``{True}``"
msgstr "``{True}``"

#: ../../../builtins-hard.rst:286
#, python-brace-format
msgid "``{1.0}``"
msgstr "``{1.0}``"

#: ../../../builtins-hard.rst:287
#, python-brace-format
msgid "``{1}``"
msgstr "``{1}``"

#: ../../../builtins-hard.rst:292
msgid ""
"``1``, ``True`` and ``1.0`` are all equal and hash the same, so the set "
"keeps only the first one inserted — the integer ``1``."
msgstr ""
"``1``, ``True`` y ``1.0`` son todos iguales y tienen el mismo hash, así que "
"el conjunto conserva solo el primero insertado — el entero ``1``."

#: ../../../builtins-hard.rst:311 ../../../builtins-hard.rst:440
#: ../../../builtins-hard.rst:465
msgid "``None``"
msgstr "``None``"

#: ../../../builtins-hard.rst:317
msgid ""
"``all`` is *vacuously* true on an empty iterable: there is no element that "
"fails, so it returns ``True``. (``any([])`` is the mirror image and returns "
"``False``.)"
msgstr ""
"``all`` es *vacuamente* verdadero sobre un iterable vacío: no hay ningún "
"elemento que falle, así que devuelve ``True``. (``any([])`` es el caso "
"simétrico y devuelve ``False``.)"

#: ../../../builtins-hard.rst:335
msgid "``1010``"
msgstr "``1010``"

#: ../../../builtins-hard.rst:336
msgid "``0b1010``"
msgstr "``0b1010``"

#: ../../../builtins-hard.rst:337
msgid "``'0b1010'``"
msgstr "``'0b1010'``"

#: ../../../builtins-hard.rst:338
msgid "``b'1010'``"
msgstr "``b'1010'``"

#: ../../../builtins-hard.rst:343
msgid ""
"``bin`` returns a *string* with a ``0b`` prefix. ``print`` shows the string "
"content without quotes, so the output is ``0b1010``."
msgstr ""
"``bin`` devuelve una *cadena* con el prefijo ``0b``. ``print`` muestra el "
"contenido de la cadena sin comillas, así que la salida es ``0b1010``."

#: ../../../builtins-hard.rst:360
msgid "``3``"
msgstr "``3``"

#: ../../../builtins-hard.rst:361
msgid "``6``"
msgstr "``6``"

#: ../../../builtins-hard.rst:362
msgid "``4``"
msgstr "``4``"

#: ../../../builtins-hard.rst:363
msgid "``5``"
msgstr "``5``"

#: ../../../builtins-hard.rst:368
msgid ""
"``len`` on the *string* is 4 code points, but once encoded to UTF-8 the "
"``é`` takes two bytes, so the ``bytes`` object has length ``5``."
msgstr ""
"``len`` sobre la *cadena* da 4 puntos de código, pero una vez codificada en "
"UTF-8 la ``é`` ocupa dos bytes, así que el objeto ``bytes`` tiene longitud "
"``5``."

#: ../../../builtins-hard.rst:386
msgid "``31``"
msgstr "``31``"

#: ../../../builtins-hard.rst:388
msgid "``0x1f``"
msgstr "``0x1f``"

#: ../../../builtins-hard.rst:393
msgid ""
"Base ``0`` tells ``int`` to auto-detect the base from the literal prefix. "
"The ``0x`` marks hexadecimal, so ``1f`` parses to ``31``."
msgstr ""
"La base ``0`` le indica a ``int`` que detecte automáticamente la base a "
"partir del prefijo del literal. El ``0x`` indica hexadecimal, así que ``1f``"
" se analiza como ``31``."

#: ../../../builtins-hard.rst:410
msgid "``[104, 105]``"
msgstr "``[104, 105]``"

#: ../../../builtins-hard.rst:411
msgid "``'hi'``"
msgstr "``'hi'``"

#: ../../../builtins-hard.rst:412
msgid "``b'hi'``"
msgstr "``b'hi'``"

#: ../../../builtins-hard.rst:413
msgid "``b'104105'``"
msgstr "``b'104105'``"

#: ../../../builtins-hard.rst:418
msgid ""
"``bytes`` from a list of integers treats each as a byte value; ``104`` and "
"``105`` are the ASCII codes for ``h`` and ``i``, giving ``b'hi'``."
msgstr ""
"``bytes`` a partir de una lista de enteros trata cada uno como un valor de "
"byte; ``104`` y ``105`` son los códigos ASCII de ``h`` e ``i``, dando "
"``b'hi'``."

#: ../../../builtins-hard.rst:439
msgid "``256``"
msgstr "``256``"

#: ../../../builtins-hard.rst:445
msgid ""
"CPython caches small integers from ``-5`` to ``256``, so both names point at"
" the *same* cached object and ``is`` is ``True``. This is a CPython "
"implementation detail — never rely on ``is`` for value equality."
msgstr ""
"CPython cachea los enteros pequeños de ``-5`` a ``256``, así que ambos "
"nombres apuntan al *mismo* objeto cacheado e ``is`` es ``True``. Esto es un "
"detalle de implementación de CPython — nunca confíes en ``is`` para la "
"igualdad de valores."

#: ../../../builtins-hard.rst:471
msgid ""
"Unlike ``in`` on a stored object, ``list.index`` builds a *fresh* NaN to "
"search for. The two NaN objects are different, so the identity shortcut "
"fails, ``==`` is ``False``, and no match is found — ``index`` raises "
"``ValueError``."
msgstr ""
"A diferencia de ``in`` sobre un objeto almacenado, ``list.index`` construye "
"un NaN *nuevo* para buscar. Los dos objetos NaN son distintos, así que el "
"atajo por identidad falla, ``==`` es ``False`` y no se encuentra ninguna "
"coincidencia — ``index`` lanza ``ValueError``."

#: ../../../builtins-hard.rst:490
msgid "``(1, 'b')``"
msgstr "``(1, 'b')``"

#: ../../../builtins-hard.rst:491
msgid "``(1, 'a')``"
msgstr "``(1, 'a')``"

#: ../../../builtins-hard.rst:493
msgid "``(1, 'ab')``"
msgstr "``(1, 'ab')``"

#: ../../../builtins-hard.rst:498
msgid ""
"Both items have the same key (``1``). On ties, ``max`` returns the *first* "
"maximal element encountered, so ``(1, 'a')`` wins. (``min`` follows the same"
" first-wins rule.)"
msgstr ""
"Ambos elementos tienen la misma clave (``1``). En caso de empate, ``max`` "
"devuelve el *primer* elemento máximo encontrado, así que gana ``(1, 'a')``. "
"(``min`` sigue la misma regla de que gana el primero.)"

#: ../../../builtins-hard.rst:517
msgid "``2``"
msgstr "``2``"

#: ../../../builtins-hard.rst:518
msgid "``128512``"
msgstr "``128512``"

#: ../../../builtins-hard.rst:519
msgid "``55357``"
msgstr "``55357``"

#: ../../../builtins-hard.rst:524
msgid ""
"``ord`` accepts any single Unicode *code point*, including astral-plane "
"emoji. ``😀`` is U+1F600, whose decimal value is ``128512`` — Python strings "
"are not UTF-16, so there is no surrogate pair to trip over."
msgstr ""
"``ord`` acepta cualquier *punto de código* Unicode individual, incluidos los"
" emoji del plano astral. ``😀`` es U+1F600, cuyo valor decimal es ``128512`` "
"— las cadenas de Python no son UTF-16, así que no hay ningún par suplente "
"con el que tropezar."
